{"title":"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Answer\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Answer</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> denote the set of nonnegative integers.  Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> to itself such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1c7297b8725e7d5c85d5067c624a51fdc4180c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m+f(n))=f(f(m))+f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"249\" height=\"20\" />      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8a147b8ccdd97022aeb67571146bb18d5c40f6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall m,n \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Answer\">Answer</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Answer\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two general solutions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57ccf8d123ba4259e29fba55d9b008874e071492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> (where the only fixed point is 0) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6bdd305ed9ff9a7cdc5a6914902da258f08af5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = n_{0}\\dot(a_{r} + q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"24\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f203b6a1685d7670fc9e8e751d5984526f17ae4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is the smallest fixed point greater than 0 (in the second case), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f86549e6060ec8fe2718a61c52129fbb21553cc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r) = a_{r}n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e21d5ce5416c138f2029c9f35e592e292af800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> and q is the quotient when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f203b6a1685d7670fc9e8e751d5984526f17ae4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Plugging in m = 0, we get f(f(n)) = f(n) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39de36afb864dd5fd88b73e765ed0f0f6178f405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall n \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />. \nWith m = n = 0, we get f(0) = 0.\n</p><p>If there are no fixed points of this function greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740a347acb5d6cc05d0385ba56b763a44f097cbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 0 \\forall x \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />, which is a valid solution.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f203b6a1685d7670fc9e8e751d5984526f17ae4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb0cfbaf68f5a7f8a348ea2b8ec5651ff0cc8f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/39902d1c80136d3437350a8fd46577964592b10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies f(n_{0}) = n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />. \nPlugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf72c53642b9d22319b6e64b5e104bd54f0394e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = n = n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db24c1f71646ee0bc4b42dbb8c3e64819adcd22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2n_{0}) = 2f(n_{0})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nBy an easy induction, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b95a7d9a6c835e6a8142d25d9fa874ba443b34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(kn_{0}) = kf(n_{0}) \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac21748a7f4197c82a42b26648f7fb7796be070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> be another fixed point greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f203b6a1685d7670fc9e8e751d5984526f17ae4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddff0a62c99f0938ec0bcec085619e927b4d3ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{1} = qn_{0} + r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e21d5ce5416c138f2029c9f35e592e292af800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/8998800d2d3cf19ec025e17b26924f94886de1bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n_{1}) = f(qn_{0} + r) = f(r + f(qn_{0})) = f(r) + qn_{0} = r + qn_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"474\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a607f051fd6558ced4d1824a407bcc8bc6c53a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies f(r) = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />. But, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/40665c5d3230f606fcfc852982658ca8cad26a9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; n_{0} \\implies r = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"17\" />. This means that the set of all fixed points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df621a5348c783a5656893bb39724328b14639be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${0, n_{0}, 2n_{0}, 3n{0}, ...}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/616eec2445bffcd937c88220f258549109abe173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13aedeb9b424113fe1e2a0587a52f05e84a4c34f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c9877645426ee65bfe80854c6b513e5035648d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = f(x) = f(f(x)) = f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is also a fixed point, which means that the functional values of non-fixed points are permutations of the fixed points. So let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1d09f2161d4e67e5978a177871af3e5ee3fb710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k) = a_{k}n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e04d02669555107dfe445dff76e63a62c60e9a5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k} \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNow let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390fe552ca378aabba3db6f0ecc3121fb4d0faf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = qn_{0} + r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e21d5ce5416c138f2029c9f35e592e292af800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />.\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e53bfd138e8545ab3ea1c3850c3e6bb7712362c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = f(qn_{0} + r) = f(r + f(qn_{0})) = f(r) + f(qn_{0}) = f(r) + qn_{0} = a_{r}n_{0} + qn_{0} = n_{0}\\dot(a_{r} + q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"731\" height=\"24\" />.\nSo there are two general solutions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57ccf8d123ba4259e29fba55d9b008874e071492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> (where the only fixed point is 0) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6bdd305ed9ff9a7cdc5a6914902da258f08af5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = n_{0}\\dot(a_{r} + q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"24\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f203b6a1685d7670fc9e8e751d5984526f17ae4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is the smallest fixed point greater than 0 (in the second case), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f86549e6060ec8fe2718a61c52129fbb21553cc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r) = a_{r}n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e21d5ce5416c138f2029c9f35e592e292af800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> and q is the quotient when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f203b6a1685d7670fc9e8e751d5984526f17ae4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO\" title=\"1996 IMO\">1996 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185944\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 273/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8789/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.651      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.651      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25394:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017185944 and revision id 292307. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}